  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study Critical Raw Materials South Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With South Africa being a significant player in global mining and mineral processing, there is a growing demand for Critical Raw Materials (CRMs) essential for high-tech products and sustainable transitions. This demand presents opportunities for South Africa to focus on value addition and downstream processing of CRMs, fostering industries like battery manufacturing and renewable energy technologies while promoting job creation locally. However, the CRM sector also poses challenges, such as negative environmental impacts and energy and water-intensive processes. Sustainable extraction and processing methods are crucial, requiring innovation, new technologies, and expertise. In this project, a study will be conducted to identify avenues for mutually beneficial collaboration between South Africa and the Netherlands in developing sustainable CRM value chains. The objective of the study is to 1)	Analyse and identify the synergies between the Netherlands&apos; and South Africa&#x2019;s strategic CRM interests and capabilities; 2)	Identify the key stakeholders in South Africa&#x2019;s CRM sector; and 3)	Develop recommendations for collaboration between South Africa and the Netherlands in the CRM sector.</narrative>
  </description>
